.\"  -*- nroff -*-
.TH OWNTONE "8" "2026-10" "owntone-mini" "AirPlay audio sender"
.SH NAME
owntone \- AirPlay audio sender fed from a pipe (owntone-mini)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B owntone
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBowntone\fP is the daemon of owntone-mini, a minimal fork of OwnTone.
It reads audio from a named pipe (FIFO) and streams it to AirPlay 1 and
AirPlay 2 speakers on the local network. The binary is called
\fBowntone\fP; the package is called owntone-mini.
.PP
The daemon is controlled through an HTTP JSON API. Its settings are kept in a
JSON file, which is created with defaults on first start if it does not
exist. See the project documentation for the settings and the API.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-debug=\fR\fIlevel\fP
Log level, a number from 0 to 5: 0 fatal, 1 log, 2 warning, 3 info, 4 debug,
5 spam. Each level includes the lower ones. If not given, the \fIloglevel\fP
setting is used (default 3).
.TP
\fB\-D, \-\-logdomains=\fR\fIdom,..,dom\fP
Restrict logging to the listed domains, separated by commas or spaces.
Available domains are: \fIconfig\fP, \fIhttpd\fP, \fImain\fP, \fImdns\fP,
\fImisc\fP, \fIxcode\fP, \fIevent\fP, \fIffmpeg\fP, \fIplayer\fP,
\fIraop\fP, \fIdacp\fP, \fIweb\fP, \fIairplay\fP. An unknown domain is an
error. If not given, all domains are logged.
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-foreground\fR
Run in the foreground instead of as a background daemon.
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-config=\fR\fIfile\fP
Use \fIfile\fP as the settings file.
.TP
\fB\-P, \-\-pidfile=\fR\fIfile\fP
Write the process ID to \fIfile\fP.
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-logformat=\fR\fIformat\fP
Log line format: \fIdefault\fP or \fIlogfmt\fP. Any other value selects
\fIdefault\fP. If not given, the \fIlogformat\fP setting is used.
.SH FILES
.nf
 \fI/etc/owntone-settings.json\fR  settings file (default; set with \fB\-c\fR)
 \fI/var/log/owntone.log\fR  log file (default; set by the \fIlogfile\fP setting)
 \fI/var/run/owntone.pid\fR  PID file (default; set with \fB\-P\fR)
.fi
.PP
The default settings and PID file locations follow the directories chosen when
owntone-mini was built.
